# GitHub App OAuth Configuration
# 
# To set up GitHub App OAuth:
# 
# 1. Go to https://github.com/settings/apps/new
# 2. Fill in the form:
#    - App name: STF-Workbench-Dev (or similar)
#    - Homepage URL: http://localhost:5173
#    - Callback URL: http://localhost:8000/auth/github/callback
#    - Webhook URL: (leave empty for now)
#    - Permissions:
#      - Contents: Read & Write (to manage repos)
#      - Pull Requests: Read & Write (to create/merge PRs)
#      - Workflows: Read & Write (to manage GitHub Actions)
#    - Events: None for now
#    - Where can this app be installed: Only on this account
# 3. After creation, copy these values from the app settings:
#    - App ID: (from About section)
#    - Private key: Generate new private key (save as .pem file)
#    - Client ID: (from About section)
#    - Client secret: Generate new client secret
# 4. Create .env file in the project root with values below

# GitHub App ID (integer)
GITHUB_APP_ID=xxxxxxxx

# GitHub App private key (full RSA private key as string, may include newlines)
# Copy the entire .pem file content
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----
-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----


# GitHub OAuth Client ID
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxx

# GitHub OAuth Client Secret
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxx

# OAuth redirect URI (must match GitHub App settings)
GITHUB_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8000/auth/github/callback
